H-OVERBLOCK (Enigma) — NOT SHIPPED: no win. Against main dc44922 (v6.14).
Rule: nextBlocker declares no hand blocker when a defence reaction in hand/arsenal
(judge.defendsNow) prints defence >= the whole leak and its printed cost is payable from
floating resources + the free hand's pitch; not on a lethal hit. Gate SPXOVERBLOCK, key
blockRxCovers, drill test/overblock.test.js (gate off fails it).
Own-seat A/B, Enigma vs the 14 others, both seat orders, 28 games/seed, 12 seeds paired:
  rule policy: 15.58 -> 16.25 (+0.67, t 1.08)   per seed 16→16 14→13 13→14 15→16 14→13 15→15 21→17 13→16 17→20 16→20 17→18 16→17
  Sharp (Enigma's seat), this patch: 21.42 -> 21.58 (+0.17, t 0.39)
  Sharp with ALSO a filter on laBlockSets (drop sets holding a hand card a reaction covers):
               21.42 -> 19.58 (-1.83, t -3.19) — removed; the search's own block sets know better.
Census: the rule policy meets this case in ~4% of its hand blocks, mostly lethal (excluded) or
the reaction unpayable once the card is kept; Sharp meets it in ~10% (11 of 107 over 8 games).
0 refusals / violations / stalls in every A/B run. Full ladder not run (not shipping).
Apply: git apply experiments/spxoverblock.patch

